From: MoveCertificate contributors
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: do not copy DRM syncobj payloads on kbase

Kbase uses CPU sync objects and KCPU sync_file exports, not DRM syncobjs.
The inherited copy_sync_payloads hook makes Android image release invoke
DRM_IOCTL_SYNCOBJ_HANDLE_TO_FD on /dev/mali0 and fail with ENOTTY.
Leave the hook unset for kbase so the common Android runtime uses its
QueueSubmit2 fallback and the existing kbase semaphore export implementation.
Keep the DRM backend unchanged. Apply after the pinned RC3 upstream series.

--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
@@ -385,7 +385,13 @@
    device->vk.shader_ops = &panvk_per_arch(device_shader_ops);
    device->vk.check_status = panvk_device_check_status;
    device->vk.get_timestamp = panvk_device_get_timestamp;
-   device->vk.copy_sync_payloads = vk_drm_syncobj_copy_payloads;
+#ifdef HAVE_PAN_KMOD_KBASE
+   /* Kbase sync objects cannot be passed to the DRM payload-copy helper.
+    * A NULL hook selects the common QueueSubmit2 synchronization path.
+    */
+   if (!physical_device->kbase_node_path[0])
+#endif
+      device->vk.copy_sync_payloads = vk_drm_syncobj_copy_payloads;
 
    device->kmod.allocator = (struct pan_kmod_allocator){
       .zalloc = panvk_kmod_zalloc,
